---@field apiFunctionalRequirements? gcp.apihub_v1.GoogleCloudApihubV1AttributeValues Optional. The api functional requirements associated with the API resource. Cardinality is 1 for this attribute. This maps to the following system defined attribute: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/attributes/system-api-functional-requirements` attribute. The value of the attribute should be a proper URI, and in case of Cloud Storage URI, it should point to a Cloud Storage object, not a directory.
---@field serviceType? gcp.apihub_v1.GoogleCloudApihubV1AttributeValues Optional. The type of the service. This maps to the following system defined attribute: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/attributes/system-service-type` attribute. The cardinality of this attribute is 1. All values should be from the list of allowed values defined for the attribute.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. The time at which the API resource was last updated.
---@field apiTechnicalRequirements? gcp.apihub_v1.GoogleCloudApihubV1AttributeValues Optional. The api technical requirements associated with the API resource. Cardinality is 1 for this attribute. This maps to the following system defined attribute: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/attributes/system-api-technical-requirements` attribute. The value of the attribute should be a proper URI, and in case of Cloud Storage URI, it should point to a Cloud Storage object, not a directory.
---@field team? gcp.apihub_v1.GoogleCloudApihubV1AttributeValues Optional. The team owning the API. This maps to the following system defined attribute: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/attributes/system-team` attribute. The number of values for this attribute will be based on the cardinality of the attribute. The same can be retrieved via GetAttribute API. All values should be from the list of allowed values defined for the attribute.
---@field apiRequirements? gcp.apihub_v1.GoogleCloudApihubV1AttributeValues Optional. The api requirement doc associated with the API resource. Cardinality is 1 for this attribute. This maps to the following system defined attribute: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/attributes/system-api-requirements` attribute. The value of the attribute should be a proper URI, and in case of Cloud Storage URI, it should point to a Cloud Storage object, not a directory.
---@field attributes? gcp.apihub_v1.GoogleCloudApihubV1AttributeValuesMap Optional. The list of user defined attributes associated with the API resource. The key is the attribute name. It will be of the format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/attributes/{attribute}`. The value is the attribute values associated with the resource.
---@field targetUser? gcp.apihub_v1.GoogleCloudApihubV1AttributeValues Optional. The target users for the API. This maps to the following system defined attribute: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/attributes/system-target-user` attribute. The number of values for this attribute will be based on the cardinality of the attribute. The same can be retrieved via GetAttribute API. All values should be from the list of allowed values defined for the attribute.
---@field displayName? string Required. The display name of the API resource.
---@field selectedVersion? string Optional. The selected version for an API resource. This can be used when special handling is needed on client side for particular version of the API. Format is `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/apis/{api}/versions/{version}`
---@field sourceMetadata? gcp.apihub_v1.GoogleCloudApihubV1SourceMetadataList Output only. The list of sources and metadata from the sources of the API resource.
---@field maturityLevel? gcp.apihub_v1.GoogleCloudApihubV1AttributeValues Optional. The maturity level of the API. This maps to the following system defined attribute: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/attributes/system-maturity-level` attribute. The number of values for this attribute will be based on the cardinality of the attribute. The same can be retrieved via GetAttribute API. All values should be from the list of allowed values defined for the attribute.
---@field businessUnit? gcp.apihub_v1.GoogleCloudApihubV1AttributeValues Optional. The business unit owning the API. This maps to the following system defined attribute: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/attributes/system-business-unit` attribute. The number of values for this attribute will be based on the cardinality of the attribute. The same can be retrieved via GetAttribute API. All values should be from the list of allowed values defined for the attribute.
